 # Changelog
 
+## 1.5.0 (2026-11-22)
+
+- Ticket assignment. `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` with `{"assignee": "Ada Lovelace"}` assigns an open or in-progress
+  ticket to an agent, and `{"assignee": null}` unassigns it; a resolved or closed ticket is 409 `conflict`. Assigning
+  the agent the ticket already has changes nothing. Every ticket has an `assignee`, `null` when it is unassigned, and
+  keeps it when it is resolved, closed or reopened.
+- The agent a ticket is assigned to is notified (`ticket.assigned`, addressed to the agent's name as assigned). Every
+  actual assignment has its own notification, delivered even if the ticket is reassigned or unassigned before it goes
+  out. Unassigning notifies no one. Both are recorded in the audit log as `ticket.assigned`.
+- `GET /tickets?assignee=Ada%20Lovelace` lists that agent's tickets and `?assignee=` the unassigned ones.
+- Filters combine as documented: a ticket is listed only when it matches every filter given (1.4.0 listed a ticket
+  that matched any one of them). A filter given more than once must match each of its values, so two different values
+  list nothing.
+- The command line's `list` and `show` print the assignee; `list --raw` adds it as a fifth column, after the four the
+  weekly report reads.
+- Text limits count Unicode code points, so a character such as `𠮷` or `😀` counts as one, not two, and text that is
+  not valid Unicode is `invalid`: for titles and requesters as for agent names.
+- When the data file cannot be written, a `PATCH`, a transition or an assignment is answered 500 and not made, so the
+  same request sent again saves it. Before, the change stayed in the running service without being saved, and the same
+  request sent again did not save it: it answered 200 for an assignment or a `PATCH`, and 409 for a transition.
+- The data file is still version 1; a ticket saved without an `assignee` loads as unassigned.
+
 ## 1.4.0 (2025-09-15)
 
 - The operator command line, `bin/tickets.js` (`list`, `show`), and the weekly report, `scripts/weekly-report.js`.
